## if_on_an_int (exit 1)
error[Z0203]: `if` needs one Bool, but `1` is an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:4
  |
1 | if 1 { 2 }
  |    ^ not a Bool
  |
  = help: write a comparison, `wages.n_rows() < 30`, or a binding that holds a Bool

## if_on_text (exit 1)
error[Z0203]: `if` needs one Bool, but `"yes"` is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:4
  |
1 | if "yes" { 2 }
  |    ^^^^^ not a Bool
  |
  = help: write a comparison, `wages.n_rows() < 30`, or a binding that holds a Bool

## if_on_a_column (exit 1)
error[Z0203]: `if` needs one Bool, but `d["x"] > 1` is a Bool column
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:4
  |
2 | if d["x"] > 1 { 2 }
  |    ^^^^^^^^^^ a column, not one value
  |
  = help: `if` decides what the script does and takes one Bool; a value chosen row by row is a `case`: `case { condition => a, _ => b }` (section 5.1)

## if_on_na (exit 1)
error[Z0203]: `if` needs one Bool, but the condition is NA
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:4
  |
1 | if [NA, true][1] { 2 }
  |    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ NA decides nothing
  |
  = help: an `NA` condition is neither true nor false; test it first with `is_missing`, or give the comparison a value with `coalesce`

## if_on_a_column_found_at_run_time (exit 1)
warning: `x` is both a variable of d and a binding; the variable was used (line 3)
  = help: rename the binding, or write `d["x"]` and the binding apart; inside a frame method a bare name is the frame's variable first
error[Z0203]: `if` needs one Bool, but `x` is an Int column
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:14
  |
3 | d.add(y = if x { 1 } else { 0 })
  |              ^ a column, not one value
  |
  = help: `if` decides what the script does and takes one Bool; a value chosen row by row is a `case`: `case { condition => a, _ => b }` (section 5.1)

## if_without_else_bound (exit 1)
error[Z0206]: this gives no value, so it cannot be bound
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:9
  |
1 | let x = if true { 1 }
  |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ its type is Nothing
  |
  = help: an `if` without `else` is a statement and gives nothing; add an `else` branch to use it as a value (section 3.7)

## if_on_nothing (exit 1)
error[Z0206]: this gives no value, so it cannot be used as a condition
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:4
  |
1 | if print(1) { 2 }
  |    ^^^^^^^^ its type is Nothing
  |
  = help: `print` and the other statements that print or warn return nothing; use the value they were given

## if_branches_differ (exit 1)
error[Z0214]: the branches of an `if` must give one type: this one has an Int and a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:28
  |
1 | let x = if true { 1 } else { "a" }
  |                 ----- an Int
  |                            ^^^^^^^ a Str
  |
  = help: Int and Float join as Float and NA fits any type; other types need a conversion, `to(x, Str)`

## if_branch_without_a_value (exit 1)
error[Z0206]: this gives no value, so it cannot be bound
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:9
  |
1 | let x = if true { let y = 1 } else { 2 }
  |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ its type is Nothing
  |
  = help: an `if` is a value only when every branch ends in a value, the last `else` included; one of these gives nothing (section 3.1, "Value of a block")

## case_arm_not_a_condition (exit 1)
error[Z0203]: a `case` arm's condition must be a Bool or a Bool column, but `1` is an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:8
  |
1 | case { 1 => 2, _ => 3 }
  |        ^ not a condition
  |
  = help: write a comparison, `age < 25`, or a Bool variable; the catch-all is `_`

## case_arms_differ (exit 1)
error[Z0214]: the arms of a `case` must give one type: this one has a Str after an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:25
  |
1 | case { 1 < 2 => 1, _ => "a" }
  |                         ^^^ a Str
  |
  = help: Int and Float join as Float and NA fits any type; other types need a conversion, `to(x, Str)`

## case_arm_gives_nothing (exit 1)
error[Z0206]: this gives no value, so it cannot be the value of a `case` arm
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:17
  |
1 | case { 1 < 2 => print(1), _ => 2 }
  |                 ^^^^^^^^ its type is Nothing
  |
  = help: `print` and the other statements that print or warn return nothing; use the value they were given

## case_catch_all_first (exit 1)
error[Z0316]: `_` may appear once in a `case`, and only as the last arm
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:8
  |
1 | case { _ => 1, true => 2 }
  |        ^^^^^^ arms after this one can never be reached
  |
  = help: put the `_` arm last

## case_empty (exit 1)
error[Z0301]: a `case` needs at least one arm
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | case { }
  | ^^^^^^^^ no arm between the braces
  |
  = help: write `case { condition => value, _ => other }`

## case_unreachable_arm (exit 0)
1
warning[W0301]: this condition is always true, so the arms after it can never be reached
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:8
  |
1 | case { true => 1, false => 2 }
  |        ^^^^ `true` matches every row
  |
  = help: write the catch-all as the last arm, `_ => value`, or remove the arms after this one

